  "description": "Mermaid diagrams (Q-D12, step 9, research/14 §6.21). The runtime Mermaid checks (tests/runtime/lib/mermaid.mjs) render every block of `note` twice in the isolated Obsidian: as Obsidian draws it with the theme applied, and as a REFERENCE -- the same text, the same bundled Mermaid, the base theme and themeVariables resolved from this theme's --ink-mermaid-* tokens, which is what Inkdrop's Mermaid plugin does (inkdropapp/mermaid@384e9f5 packages/mermaid/src/theme.ts). `tokens` maps each themeVariable to the --ink-mermaid-<token> that Inkdrop's theme.ts reads it from (--mermaid-<token>), limited to the ones the palette declares; Mermaid derives the rest from them as in Inkdrop. `kinds` are the supported diagram kinds (svg[aria-roledescription]); `unsupported` the other kinds of the note, which keep Obsidian's inverting filter and are reported as UNSUPPORTED, never PASS. `image` is the note's test image, whose filter must stay none. `required` lists, per kind, element types (a tag and classes it must have) of which at least one element must be drawn, over all blocks of that kind.",
